er/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/assets/8361d4cb197686b79cf21cb88ee70de5b3578e92fb758fb84aec754871dfca3e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115699/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "39fe786b-4764-590d-b275-6412c661af10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115699/selection/1fa5ed823ab38ae7efbf795cb4140fd76565ae5c293c73ca2dd6ddbbf57f22fe" :answer-field/choices ["q-115699/selection/4298c7cb70e95faee4a43d49ed01733c7ddb6793f0891654b4d46609c3da3ba7" "q-115699/selection/421c42540d2f0ee579c9e93a6dc606f5384abba37c7fcd45330210179fed7c7c" "q-115699/selection/db3090c1a1b2996a5ed0c4ce7420ee60ff8b263b5c31f0d06d1a6db3cdc80b0c" "q-115699/selection/b3dc9b75eb3251d978aa963accdec69e7ce1e3db9d6a1da96202e67d67433b75" "q-115699/selection/1fa5ed823ab38ae7efbf795cb4140fd76565ae5c293c73ca2dd6ddbbf57f22fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115699" :question/id #uuid "73a107f3-de5c-51c5-9778-c2302ba770ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-115699" :question/problem "A right Riemann sum is used to approximate the area under the curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=-4$ and $x=-1$ for each of the functions below. For which function does the Riemann sum give an *underestimate* of the area?" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum underestimates the area under the respective curve if the function is decreasing over the given interval. \n\nOf the given options, the only function that is decreasing over $x\\in [-4,-1]$ is as follows.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038872/assets/8361d4cb197686b79cf21cb88ee70de5b3578e92fb758fb84aec754871dfca3e.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115699/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad9b9344-1711-5ff4-b489-f6ef2a0bd2eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115699"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142835/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "bbd030d7-e3f3-5d11-a24e-1a39bd081e7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142835/selection/bacb644dcae25d563be168ca23fe4c5c1c8292e9ac2cb504ba4b1b351f9a07de" :answer/id #uuid "a85045ce-0e2b-583c-bb65-24f96d61b1b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142835/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "3b7551bf-7805-5d9d-8ec0-f2ca0e1720cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142835/selection/2c81c49ac1d2e2d036da8c610f8f1fdc59a398b6553a89e243b486e49af69965" :answer/id #uuid "d211f02d-c40f-50c2-a20d-deb0a43d3209" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142835/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "35ed506a-9521-5180-a96f-682b0dd8d833" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142835/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d308c519-f561-5b02-8c0f-0dd415d40d2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-142835/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-142835/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-142835/selection/bacb644dcae25d563be168ca23fe4c5c1c8292e9ac2cb504ba4b1b351f9a07de" "q-142835/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-142835/selection/2c81c49ac1d2e2d036da8c610f8f1fdc59a398b6553a89e243b486e49af69965" "q-142835/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142835" :question/id #uuid "d7b1e141-0f1f-5182-b6a5-be50ff0bb0dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-142835" :question/problem "$\\frac{2{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\,{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{2\\,(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)-1}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+2{tan}^{2}⁡x-1}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x}}{\\cancel{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x}=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-142835/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7640012b-79f9-5f6b-a26b-a7f4fe8c0e7b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142835"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-242909/field-1/43e82907ca82ac21fc305afb2f4f415ed4304969209ab79f844f804dc4e26540" :answer/id #uuid "186858b9-b9f0-5d60-9d72-9f09ea351310" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\ln(9)}{1+\\ln(9)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-242909/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "98ddf865-1c62-526a-98a9-cb3cdff75bd0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-242909/field-1/43e82907ca82ac21fc305afb2f4f415ed4304969209ab79f844f804dc4e26540" :answer-field/choices ["q-242909/field-1/43e82907ca82ac21fc305afb2f4f415ed4304969209ab79f844f804dc4e26540"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-242909" :question/id #uuid "b74609cf-54a2-5e61-b71b-f371e006d3b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-242909" :question/problem "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, determine the value of $x$ that satisfies the equation ${e}^{x}={9}^{5-x}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x} & ={9}^{5-x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({9}^{5-x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({9}^{5-x}).\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\nx=(5-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =(5-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9) \\\\ x & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9) \\\\ x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9) & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9) \\\\ x(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)) & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9) \\\\ x & =\\frac{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)}{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-242909/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eb24b54-bdb8-5269-bd38-d346a52bbc6e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-242909"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
